# M11.2d (docs/CLI.md, docs/M11_PLAN.md section 31): the title menu's QUIT GAME -- the last item (the PS3's INSTALL's
# place, renamed). Down to it (QUIT=down presses: 3 from CONTINUE, on the normal title and on a cleared game's title,
# whose cursor also starts on CONTINUE, the third of six), CROSS: the question opens over the title with Cancel focused; CROSS takes
# Cancel (the default: No) and the title is back; CROSS on QUIT GAME again, RIGHT to Quit, CROSS: the game ends in
# order (B-010), status 0. tests/title_quit.py runs it on both titles and reads the log. The question is the in-game
# menu's: a test answers it through overlay.input (DOTHEROES_OVERLAY_TEST; a drive's presses reach the game's pad, the
# menu reads the host's controller and keyboard).
#! env DOTHEROES_OVERLAY_TEST=1
log TitleMovie 120
sleep 5
press START                 # "PRESS START BUTTON" -> the menu, CONTINUE (a save is there)
sleep 4
shot menu
loop ${QUIT:-3}
  press DOWN
  sleep 1
end
sleep 2
shot menu-quit
press CROSS                 # QUIT GAME: the question
sleep 3
shot question
write overlay.input a       # Cancel (focused): back to the title
sleep 3
shot cancelled
press CROSS                 # QUIT GAME again (the cursor stayed on it)
sleep 3
shot question-again
write overlay.input right   # Quit
sleep 1
shot quit-focused
write overlay.input a       # the game ends
sleep 10
shot after
